Z||000000||87ECO5||09-29-2000||12:48 PM||||Just got the newest <B>Car and Driver</B> in the mail.  If you haven't seen it yet, check out page 32.  Yep, it's a "minitest" on the Speedster.<P>As you read through it, you'll notice they mention just about every two-seater under the sun.  As I did, you'll begin to shake with anticipation.  Then finally, they hit you - HARD!:<P><B>"Now for the big question:  Will the Speedster come to America, perhaps as a resurrected Fiero?"</B><P>At this point, if you're anything like me, you're leaping out of your chair, screaming at anyone that can hear you - "They mentioned our car!!!!!"<P>Unfortunately, they slam you back down in your seat - rather abruptly:<P><B>"Let us answer that succinctly:  Is crack cocaine a healthy way to lose weight?"</B>  Well, it depends on who you ask, right!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'll admit I was disappointed - AGAIN!  I knew they weren't bringing it over but hearing it again was like someone tearing open a freshly-healed wound!  Then I read more of the article.  They go on to say the car offers little to no creature comforts to go with its $30,000 price tag and its build quality is questionable.  Two drawbacks that would have its competitors eating it alive!<P>Long live the Fiero!||||reg||13
